# text = Tulliver said Mr . Tulliver , winking and smiling at Mr . Riley , with the natural pride of a man who has a buxom wife conspicuously his inferior in intellect said Mr . Riley , quietly said Mr . Tulliver broke in Maggie , who had stolen unperceived to her father's elbow again , listening with parted lips , while she held her doll topsy-turvy , and crushed its nose against the wood of the chair said the father , tenderly Maggie came round promptly in front of Mr . Riley , and said that gentleman answered , being of opinion that children , when they are not naughty , should always be spoken to jocosely said Maggie , tossing her head haughtily , and turning away , with the tears springing in her eyes .
