# text = Mr . Riley liked such men , quite apart from any money which might be diverted , through their good judgment , from less worthy pockets into his own ; and it would be a satisfaction to him to say to Timpson on his return home Timpson had a large family of daughters ; Mr . Riley felt for him ; besides , Louisa Timpson's face , with its light curls , had been a familiar object to him over the pew wainscot on a Sunday for nearly fifteen years ; it was natural her husband should be a commendable tutor .
