# text = He drew something half out of his right-hand pocket said Maggie , in a whisper said Maggie , impatiently said Tom , thrusting his hand back into his pocket and looking determined said Maggie , imploringly , laying hold of the arm that was held stiffly in the pocket Tom's arm slowly relaxed , and he said Maggie's answer was to throw her arms round Tom's neck and hug him , and hold her cheek against his without speaking , while he slowly unwound some of the line , saying , after a pause Tom had put the line back in his pocket , and was looking at the hooks one by one , before he spoke again said Tom , putting up the hooks again , taking out a large pocket-knife , and slowly opening the largest blade , which he looked at meditatively as he rubbed his finger along it .
