# text = Maggie felt sure that Bob was wicked , without very distinctly knowing why ; unless it was because Bob's mother was a dreadfully large fat woman , who lived at a queer round house down the river ; and once , when Maggie and Tom had wandered thither , there rushed out a brindled dog that wouldn't stop barking ; and when Bob's mother came out after it , and screamed above the barking to tell them not to be frightened , Maggie thought she was scolding them fiercely , and her heart beat with terror .
