# text = He was the first to give utterance to his astonishment he said , with an amazed twinkling in his eyes , looking at Mr . Glegg and Mr . Deane , to see if they showed any signs of comprehension said poor Mr . Tulliver , who , in the maze of this puzzling world , laid hold of any clue with great readiness and tenacity he concluded , in a tone of decision , tapping his snuff-box and taking a pinch said Mr . Deane , taking snuff vigorously , as he always did when wishing to maintain a neutral position said Mr . Glegg , who was fond of his jest , and having retired from business , felt that it was not only allowable but becoming in him to take a playful view of things said Mr .
