# text = Tulliver's mind , and she mounted the horse-block to satisfy herself by a sight of that fatal child , while Tom walked -- not very quickly -- on his way toward her she said aloud , without reflecting that there was no one to hear her But when she not only failed to discern Maggie , but presently saw Tom returning from the pool alone , this hovering fear entered and took complete possession of her , and she hurried to meet him said Tom You may conceive the terrified search for Maggie , and the difficulty of convincing her mother that she was not in the pond .
