# text = The shadow of the Saxon hero-king still walks there fitfully , reviewing the scenes of his youth and love-time , and is met by the gloomier shadow of the dreadful heathen Dane , who was stabbed in the midst of his warriors by the sword of an invisible avenger , and who rises on autumn evenings like a white mist from his tumulus on the hill , and hovers in the court of the old hall by the river-side , the spot where he was thus miraculously slain in the days before the old hall was built .
