# text = Tom Tulliver , being abundant in no form of speech , did not use any metaphor to declare his views as to the nature of Latin ; he never called it an instrument of torture ; and it was not until he had got on some way in the next half-year , and in the Delectus , that he was advanced enough to call it a " bore " and At present , in relation to this demand that he should learn Latin declensions and conjugations , Tom was in a state of as blank unimaginativeness concerning the cause and tendency of his sufferings , as if he had been an innocent shrewmouse imprisoned in the split trunk of an ash-tree in order to cure lameness in cattle .
