# text = Tom was too clear-sighted not to be aware that Mr . Stelling's standard of things was quite different , was certainly something higher in the eyes of the world than that of the people he had been living amongst , and that , brought in contact with it , he , Tom Tulliver , appeared uncouth and stupid ; he was by no means indifferent to this , and his pride got into an uneasy condition which quite nullified his boyish self-satisfaction , and gave him something of the girl's susceptibility .
