# text = Presently Tom called to her Maggie obeyed , and took the open book Tom sailed along pretty well for three lines ; and Maggie was beginning to forget her office of prompter in speculating as to what _mas_ could mean , which came twice over , when he stuck fast at _Sunt etiam volucrum_ said Maggie , opening her mouth and shaking her head said Tom , very slowly , as if the next words might be expected to come sooner when he gave them this strong hint that they were waited for said Maggie , getting impatient said Tom Tom took his pencil and made several hard dots with it on his book-cover said Maggie said Maggie said Tom With some further stammering and repetition , Tom got through the next few lines he said After some whispered gabbling , assisted by the beating of his fist on the table , Tom returned the book he began said Maggie exclaimed Tom , with a derisive laugh , for Tom had learned this omitted passage for his yesterday's lesson , and a young gentleman does not require an intimate or extensive acquaintance with Latin before he can feel the pitiable absurdity of a false quantity said Maggie , pouting .
