# text = He suddenly walked across the hearth and looked over Philip's paper he exclaimed , his tongue being completely loosed by surprise and admiration said Philip said Tom , in amazement he added , reflecting that Philip might falsely suppose that he was going to if he were too frank about the imperfection of his accomplishments said Philip said Tom , beginning to have a puzzled suspicion that Philip's crooked back might be the source of remarkable faculties said Philip , smiling said Tom , lowering his voice confidentially said Philip said Tom , nodding his head sideways , as much as to say Philip felt some bitter complacency in the promising stupidity of this well-made , active-looking boy ; but made polite by his own extreme sensitiveness , as well as by his desire to conciliate , he checked his inclination to laugh , and said quietly said Tom , with a sense of disappointment Tom did not say for he was quite absorbed in the thought that Wakem's son did not seem so spiteful a fellow as might have been expected he said presently said Philip , coloring deeply said Tom , rather ashamed of himself , now he saw Philip coloring and looking uncomfortable .
