# text = He found much difficulty in adjusting his attitude of mind toward the son of Lawyer Wakem , and it had occurred to him that if Philip disliked his father , that fact might go some way toward clearing up his perplexity he said , by way of changing the subject said Philip said Tom said Philip , who had left off using his pencil , and was resting his head on one hand , while Tom was learning forward on both elbows , and looking with increasing admiration at the dog and the donkey said Tom , with strong curiosity said Tom said Philip said Tom , who had often thought he should like to resemble Sir John Crake said Philip said Tom , not with any epigrammatic intention , but with serious satisfaction at the idea that , as far as Latin was concerned , there was no hindrance to his resembling Sir John Crake said Philip , unable to choke a laugh Philip , you perceive , was not without a wish to impress the well-made barbarian with a sense of his mental superiority said Tom , who saw a vista in this direction said Tom , jumping away from the table , and stamping first with one leg and then the other he added , pausing in his stamping with a sudden alarm , lest the contrary might be possible said Philip said Philip said Tom said Tom Tom , in his turn , wished to make the balance dip in his favor .
