# text = But one afternoon , when a sudden shower of heavy rain had detained Mr . Poulter twenty minutes longer than usual at the Black Swan , the sword was brought ,-- just for Tom to look at said Tom , handling the hilt said Tom Tom gave the requisite pantomime to indicate the double enjoyment of pulling the trigger and thrusting the spear said Mr . Poulter , involuntarily falling in with Tom's enthusiasm , and drawing the sword so suddenly that Tom leaped back with much agility said Tom , a little conscious that he had not stood his ground as became an Englishman said Mr . Poulter , contemptuously said Tom said Mr . Poulter , coughing and drawing himself up , while he gave a little preliminary play to his wrist .
