# text = Maggie , in her absent way , continued to lean forward , resting on her arms and moving her feet about , while her dark eyes got more and more fixed and vacant , as if she had quite forgotten Philip and his book said Philip , after a minute or two , still leaning on his elbow and looking at her Maggie started a little on being roused from her reverie , and said Philip repeated his question she answered immediately Philip colored ; he had meant to imply , would she love him as well in spite of his deformity , and yet when she alluded to it so plainly , he winced under her pity .
