# text = The pride and obstinacy of millers and other insignificant people , whom you pass unnoticingly on the road every day , have their tragedy too ; but it is of that unwept , hidden sort that goes on from generation to generation , and leaves no record ,-- such tragedy , perhaps , as lies in the conflicts of young souls , hungry for joy , under a lot made suddenly hard to them , under the dreariness of a home where the morning brings no promise with it , and where the unexpectant discontent of worn and disappointed parents weighs on the children like a damp , thick air , in which all the functions of life are depressed ; or such tragedy as lies in the slow or sudden death that follows on a bruised passion , though it may be a death that finds only a parish funeral .
