# text = A Dodson would not be taxed with the omission of anything that was becoming , or that belonged to that eternal fitness of things which was plainly indicated in the practice of the most substantial parishioners , and in the family traditions ,-- such as obedience to parents , faithfulness to kindred , industry , rigid honesty , thrift , the thorough scouring of wooden and copper utensils , the hoarding of coins likely to disappear from the currency , the production of first-rate commodities for the market , and the general preference of whatever was home-made .
