# text = It is in the slow , changed life that follows ; in the time when sorrow has become stale , and has no longer an emotive intensity that counteracts its pain ; in the time when day follows day in dull , unexpectant sameness , and trial is a dreary routine ,-- it is then that despair threatens ; it is then that the peremptory hunger of the soul is felt , and eye and ear are strained after some unlearned secret of our existence , which shall give to endurance the nature of satisfaction .
