# text = Just where this line of bank sloped down again to the level , a by-road turned off and led to the other side of the rise , where it was broken into very capricious hollows and mounds by the working of an exhausted stone-quarry , so long exhausted that both mounds and hollows were now clothed with brambles and trees , and here and there by a stretch of grass which a few sheep kept close-nibbled .
