# text = So it has been since the days of Hecuba , and of Hector , Tamer of horses ; inside the gates , the women with streaming hair and uplifted hands offering prayers , watching the world's combat from afar , filling their long , empty days with memories and fears ; outside , the men , in fierce struggle with things divine and human , quenching memory in the stronger light of purpose , losing the sense of dread and even of wounds in the hurrying ardor of action .
