# text = She was kneeling on a footstool at Maggie's feet , after placing that dark lady in the large crimson-velvet chair said Maggie , smiling , and holding up one of Lucy's long curls , that the sunlight might shine through it said Maggie , with playful gravity said Lucy , too thoroughly preoccupied to notice Maggie's joke said Maggie , laughing said Lucy , half-penitent at this uncharitable remark said Lucy , blushing pink over brow and neck Lucy rose from her knees and went to a little distance , holding her pretty head on one side , as if she had been arranging Maggie for a portrait , and wished to judge of the general effect said Maggie , smiling languidly as she rose from her chair and looked down on her slight , aerial cousin , whose figure was quite subordinate to her faultless drapery of silk and crape .
