# text = Then , with an air of serious reflection , unfastening her large jet brooch said Maggie , seating herself submissively , while Lucy knelt again and unfastened the contemptible butterfly Maggie gave a little sigh said Lucy , pinning the large brooch below Maggie's fine throat said Maggie said Lucy , sticking the black butterfly absently in her own collar , while her eyes met Maggie's affectionately said Maggie , in one of her bursts of loving admiration said Lucy said Maggie , shaking her head slowly said Lucy , in a tone of remonstrance said Maggie , resolutely clearing away the clouds from her face with a bright smile , and throwing herself backward in her chair Maggie took up the which lay by her on the table said Lucy , going to survey the effect in the chimney-glass Lucy hurried out of the room , but Maggie did not take the opportunity of opening her book ; she let it fall on her knees , while her eyes wandered to the window , where she could see the sunshine falling on the rich clumps of spring flowers and on the long hedge of laurels , and beyond , the silvery breadth of the dear old Floss , that at this distance seemed to be sleeping in a morning holiday .
