# text = Stephen was too well bred not to seem unaware that the previous conversation could have been felt embarrassing , and at once began to talk of impersonal matters , asking Lucy if she knew when the bazaar was at length to take place , so that there might be some hope of seeing her rain the influence of her eyes on objects more grateful than those worsted flowers that were growing under her fingers said Lucy said Stephen , looking at Maggie's plain hemming said Maggie said Lucy said Maggie , looking up quietly Lucy , good and simple as she was , could not help blushing a little .
