# text = But if Maggie had been the queen of coquettes she could hardly have invented a means of giving greater piquancy to her beauty in Stephen's eyes ; I am not sure that the quiet admission of plain sewing and poverty would have done alone , but assisted by the beauty , they made Maggie more unlike other women even than she had seemed at first Maggie went on continued Lucy , turning to Stephen said Lucy , looking rather hurt said Maggie , who had let her work fall , and was listening with keen interest said Stephen said Lucy , with pretty enthusiasm said Stephen , shaking his head with sarcastic gravity said Lucy , gravely said Stephen said Lucy , her eyes brightening with a proud pleasure that made her neglect the argumentative interests of Anglicanism here Stephen drew himself up , and rubbed his large white hands over his hair with playful self-admiration said Maggie , smiling , but not looking up said Stephen he thought , while his listeners were laughing Did Lucy intend to be present at the meeting of the Book Club next week ? was the next question .
