# text = He threw himself into the chair again said Philip Philip paused , but his father was silent Wakem burst out said Philip , who had his reasons for some sympathy with this view of Tom For the first time in the dialogue , Philip lost some of his self-control , and colored with anger he said , with bitter incisiveness Wakem darted a glance of fierce question at his son ; but Philip was not looking at him , and with a certain penitent consciousness went on , in a few moments , as if in amplification of his last words said Wakem , rising again , and forgetting everything else in a burst of resentful pride , half fatherly , half personal said Philip said Wakem , rather brutally , trying to recover his previous position Wakem strode to the door , and without looking round again , banged it after him .
