# text = All well-dressed St . Ogg's and its neighborhood were there ; and it would have been worth while to come even from a distance , to see the fine old hall , with its open roof and carved oaken rafters , and great oaken folding-doors , and light shed down from a height on the many-colored show beneath ; a very quaint place , with broad faded stripes painted on the walls , and here and there a show of heraldic animals of a bristly , long-snouted character , the cherished emblems of a noble family once the seigniors of this now civic hall .
