# text = To have taken Maggie by the hand and said to have done this would have demanded courage , deep pity , self-knowledge , generous trust ; would have demanded a mind that tasted no piquancy in evil-speaking , that felt no self-exaltation in condemning , that cheated itself with no large words into the belief that life can have any moral end , any high religion , which excludes the striving after perfect truth , justice , and love toward the individual men and women who come across our own path .
