# text = But the younger generation , who had seen several small floods , thought lightly of these sombre recollections and forebodings ; and Bob Jakin , naturally prone to take a hopeful view of his own luck , laughed at his mother when she regretted their having taken a house by the riverside , observing that but for that they would have had no boats , which were the most lucky of possessions in case of a flood that obliged them to go to a distance for food .
